-- ccc6-csaem.l4 -- s 163.1, Child sexual abuse and exploitation material: the definition, the offences of making, distributing, possessing, accessing and threatening,
-- the aggravating factor, the defences and the question of law.
-- The definition ("means") is encoded closed: material outside (a) to (d) is JUST FALSE. The offences take the answer of `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` as an input.

§ `s 163.1 Child sexual abuse and exploitation material`

-- src:3227 | Definition of child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3228 | 163.1 (1) In this section, child sexual abuse and exploitation material means
-- src:3229 | (a) a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means,
-- src:3230 | (i) that shows a person who is or is depicted as being under the age of eighteen years and is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity, or
-- src:3231 | (ii) the dominant characteristic of which is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a sexual organ of a person under the age of eighteen years;
-- src:3232 | (b) any written material, visual representation or audio recording that advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act;
-- src:3233 | (c) any written material whose dominant characteristic is the description, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act; or
-- src:3234 | (d) any audio recording that has as its dominant characteristic the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(1) (src:3227-3234)
GIVEN `it is a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is written material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an audio recording` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it shows a person who is or is depicted as being under the age of eighteen years and is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a dominant characteristic of the visual representation is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a sexual organ of a person under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its dominant characteristic as written material is the description, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its dominant characteristic as an audio recording is the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF    (   `it is a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means`
          AND (   `it shows a person who is or is depicted as being under the age of eighteen years and is engaged in or is depicted as engaged in explicit sexual activity`
               OR `a dominant characteristic of the visual representation is the depiction, for a sexual purpose, of a sexual organ of a person under the age of eighteen years`))
       OR (   (   `it is written material`
               OR `it is an audio recording`
               OR `it is a photographic, film, video or other visual representation, whether or not it was made by electronic or mechanical means`)
          AND `it advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act`)
       OR (   `it is written material`
          AND `its dominant characteristic as written material is the description, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act`)
       OR (   `it is an audio recording`
          AND `its dominant characteristic as an audio recording is the description, presentation or representation, for a sexual purpose, of sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section, child sexual abuse and exploitation material means (a) a photographic, film, video or other visual representation ... (b) any written material, visual representation or audio recording that advocates or counsels ... (c) any written material whose dominant characteristic ... (d) any audio recording that has as its dominant characteristic"

DECLARE `s 163.1(2) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 163.1(2) makes`
    `s 163.1(2) prints`
    `s 163.1(2) publishes`
    `s 163.1(2) possesses for the purpose of publication`
    `s 163.1(2) none of those`

-- src:3235 | Making child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3236 | (2) Every person who makes, prints, publishes or possesses for the purpose of publication any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(2) (src:3235-3236)
GIVEN `what the person did with the material` IS A `s 163.1(2) what the person did`
      `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(2) the conduct is the offence of making, printing or publishing child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did with the material` EQUALS `s 163.1(2) none of those`)
      AND `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who makes, prints, publishes or possesses for the purpose of publication any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(2) (src:3236)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(2) the punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(2) (src:3236)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 163.1(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

DECLARE `s 163.1(3) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 163.1(3) transmits`
