-- src:3237 | Distribution, etc. of child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3238 | (3) Every person who transmits, makes available, distributes, sells, advertises, imports, exports or possesses for the purpose of transmission, making available, distribution, sale, advertising or exportation any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(3) (src:3237-3238)
GIVEN `what the person did with the material` IS A `s 163.1(3) what the person did`
      `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(3) the conduct is the offence of distributing child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did with the material` EQUALS `s 163.1(3) none of those`)
      AND `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who transmits, makes available, distributes, sells, advertises, imports, exports or possesses for the purpose of transmission, making available, distribution, sale, advertising or exportation any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of an indictable offence"

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(3) (src:3238)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(3) the punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(3) (src:3238)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 163.1(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:3239 | Possession of child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3240 | (4) Every person who possesses any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of
-- src:3241 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3242 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4) (src:3239-3242)
GIVEN `the person possesses the material` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(4) the conduct is the offence of possessing child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF `the person possesses the material` AND `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who possesses any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of"

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4)(a) (src:3241)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4)(b) (src:3242)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4) (src:3239-3242)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 163.1(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4.2) "a person accesses ... who knowingly causes ... to be viewed by, or transmitted to, himself or herself": an interpretation for (4.1), worded "who", not "means": a person outside it is NOT COVERED.
-- src:3247 | Interpretation
-- src:3248 | (4.2) For the purposes of subsection (4.1), a person accesses child sexual abuse and exploitation material who knowingly causes child sexual abuse and exploitation material to be viewed by, or transmitted to, himself or herself.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.2) (src:3247-3248)
GIVEN `the person knowingly causes child sexual abuse and exploitation material to be viewed by, or transmitted to, himself or herself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(4.2) the person accesses child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly causes child sexual abuse and exploitation material to be viewed by, or transmitted to, himself or herself`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person accesses child sexual abuse and exploitation material who knowingly causes child sexual abuse and exploitation material to be viewed by, or transmitted to, himself or herself"

-- src:3243 | Accessing child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3244 | (4.1) Every person who accesses any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of
-- src:3245 | (a) an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3246 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.1) (src:3243-3246)
GIVEN `s 163.1(4.2) the person accesses child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(4.1) the conduct is the offence of accessing child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF `s 163.1(4.2) the person accesses child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who accesses any child sexual abuse and exploitation material is guilty of"

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.1)(a) (src:3245)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4.1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.1)(b) (src:3246)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.1) (src:3243-3246)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 163.1(4.1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

DECLARE `s 163.1(4.21) what the person threatens to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 163.1(4.21) publish`
    `s 163.1(4.21) distribute`
    `s 163.1(4.21) transmit`
    `s 163.1(4.21) sell`
    `s 163.1(4.21) make available`
    `s 163.1(4.21) advertise`
    `s 163.1(4.21) nothing of that kind`

-- src:3249 | Threat to publish, etc.
-- src:3250 | (4.21) Every person who, with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously, knowingly threatens to publish, distribute, transmit, sell, make available or advertise any child sexual abuse and exploitation material
-- src:3251 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of one year; or
-- src:3252 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of six months.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.21) (src:3249-3252)
GIVEN `the person acted with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly threatened to do it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person threatens to do with the material` IS A `s 163.1(4.21) what the person threatens to do`
      `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(4.21) the conduct is the offence of threatening to publish child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously`
      AND `the person knowingly threatened to do it`
      AND NOT (`what the person threatens to do with the material` EQUALS `s 163.1(4.21) nothing of that kind`)
      AND `s 163.1(1) child sexual abuse and exploitation material` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, with the intent to intimidate or to be taken seriously, knowingly threatens to publish, distribute, transmit, sell, make available or advertise any child sexual abuse and exploitation material"

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.21)(a) (src:3251)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4.21)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.21)(b) (src:3252)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 163.1(4.21)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` `six months`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.21) (src:3249-3252)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 163.1(4.21) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (4.3) "If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence shall consider as an aggravating factor the fact that the person committed the offence with intent to make a profit."
-- A duty of the court; a failed "if" is JUST FALSE (fork F6). The same duty is a regulative rule below.
-- src:3253 | Aggravating factor
-- src:3254 | (4.3) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence shall consider as an aggravating factor the fact that the person committed the offence with intent to make a profit.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.3) (src:3253-3254)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under section 163.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person committed the offence with intent to make a profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(4.3) the court must consider the intent to make a profit as an aggravating factor` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under section 163.1` AND `the person committed the offence with intent to make a profit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence shall consider as an aggravating factor the fact that the person committed the offence with intent to make a profit"

DECLARE `s 163.1(4.3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 163.1(4.3) consider the intent to make a profit as an aggravating factor`

@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(4.3) (src:3253-3254)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 163.1(4.3) act`
`s 163.1(4.3) the sentencing court's duty to consider the intent to make a profit` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 163.1(4.3) consider the intent to make a profit as an aggravating factor`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court that imposed the sentence did not consider the intent to make a profit as an aggravating factor"

-- (5) "It is not a defence to a charge under subsection (2) in respect of a visual representation that the accused believed that a person shown in the representation ... was or was depicted as being eighteen years of age or more unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of that person and took all reasonable steps to ensure that, where the person was eighteen years of age or more, the representation did not depict that person as being under the age of eighteen years."
-- src:3255 | Defence
-- src:3256 | (5) It is not a defence to a charge under subsection (2) in respect of a visual representation that the accused believed that a person shown in the representation that is alleged to constitute child sexual abuse and exploitation material was or was depicted as being eighteen years of age or more unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of that person and took all reasonable steps to ensure that, where the person was eighteen years of age or more, the representation did not depict that person as being under the age of eighteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(5) (src:3255-3256)
GIVEN `the charge is under subsection (2) in respect of a visual representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused believed that a person shown in the representation was or was depicted as being eighteen years of age or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused took all reasonable steps to ensure that, where the person was eighteen years of age or more, the representation did not depict that person as being under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(5) the belief that the person shown was eighteen or more is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the charge is under subsection (2) in respect of a visual representation` AND `the accused believed that a person shown in the representation was or was depicted as being eighteen years of age or more`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under subsection (2) in respect of a visual representation that the accused believed that a person shown in the representation that is alleged to constitute child sexual abuse and exploitation material was or was depicted as being eighteen years of age or more"
        IF `the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of that person` AND `the accused took all reasonable steps to ensure that, where the person was eighteen years of age or more, the representation did not depict that person as being under the age of eighteen years`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the accused took all reasonable steps to ascertain the age of that person and took all reasonable steps to ensure that, where the person was eighteen years of age or more, the representation did not depict that person as being under the age of eighteen years"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3257 | Defence
-- src:3258 | (6) No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the act that is alleged to constitute the offence
-- src:3259 | (a) has a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice or to science, medicine, education or art; and
-- src:3260 | (b) does not pose an undue risk of harm to persons under the age of eighteen years.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(6) (src:3257-3260)
GIVEN `the act that is alleged to constitute the offence has a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice or to science, medicine, education or art` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act does not pose an undue risk of harm to persons under the age of eighteen years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(6) section 163.1 gives a defence` MEANS
    IF    `the act that is alleged to constitute the offence has a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice or to science, medicine, education or art`
      AND `the act does not pose an undue risk of harm to persons under the age of eighteen years`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be convicted of an offence under this section if the act that is alleged to constitute the offence (a) has a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice or to science, medicine, education or art; and (b) does not pose an undue risk of harm to persons under the age of eighteen years"

-- src:3261 | Question of law
-- src:3262 | (7) For greater certainty, for the purposes of this section, it is a question of law whether any written material, visual representation or audio recording advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 163.1(7) (src:3261-3262)
GIVEN `the question is whether any written material, visual representation or audio recording advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 163.1(7) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether any written material, visual representation or audio recording advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is a question of law whether any written material, visual representation or audio recording advocates or counsels sexual activity with a person under the age of eighteen years that would be an offence under this Act"
